  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 220°C (425°F).",
    "In a large bowl, mix together the chicken cubes, scotch bonnet peppers, garlic, olive oil, chicken seasoning, paprika, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Thread the marinated chicken onto copper skewers, leaving a small space between each piece.",
    "Place the skewers on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.",
    "Double-fry the chicken in hot oil (180°C/350°F) for 5 minutes, then set aside to cool.",
    "Increase the oven temperature to 240°C (465°F).",
    "Bake the chicken skewers for 20-25 minutes, or until crispy and cooked through.",
    "Remove the skewers from the oven and let them rest for 5 minutes before serving.",
    "Serve hot with your favorite sides."
